-- title:
--   Removing the last Taylor–Wiles prime when diamonds act trivially
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a noetherian commutative local ring that is complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with residue field $k$, let $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$, let $N,r\ge 1$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$), to $k$. Let $qv:\mathrm{Fin}(t+1)\to\mathbb{N}$ consist of primes, write $q=qv(t)$ for the last one, and put $L=N\bigl(\prod_i qv(i)\bigr)r$ and $L'=N\bigl(\prod_{i<t} qv(i)\bigr)r$; assume $q\notin S$, $q\nmid L'$ and that the image of $q$ in $k$ is $1$. Let $\alpha:\mathrm{Fin}(t+1)\to k$ satisfy $\alpha_t^2-\theta(T_q)\alpha_t+q=0$ and $2\alpha_t\neq\theta(T_q)$, i.e. $\alpha_t$ is a simple root of the $q$-th Hecke polynomial. At each of the two levels the carrier is $V_L=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_{H}(L),\mathcal{O})$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/r)^\times$, equipped with the operators indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$) and $U_i$ ($i$ ranging over $\mathrm{Fin}(t+1)$, resp. $\mathrm{Fin}(t)$); the hypotheses `hc₁`, `hc₀` assert that these operators commute pairwise at level $L$, resp. $L'$. The associated `ML` is the localisation of the carrier at the complement of the prime $\ker\tilde\theta$, where $\tilde\theta$ is the map from the free polynomial algebra $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ on those generators to $k$ sending $X_{T_\ell}\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$ and $X_{U_i}\mapsto\alpha_i$, and `toML` is the canonical map of the carrier into it. Assume that for every $u\in(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$ the diamond endomorphism $\langle u\rangle$ (conjugation by a chosen lift of $u$ in $\Gamma_0(L)$) becomes the identity after applying `toML`, and likewise at level $L'$ for every $u\in(\mathbb{Z}/L')^\times$. Then there is an $\mathcal{O}$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the localised module at level $L$ to the one at level $L'$ such that $e(X_{T_\ell}\cdot x)=X_{T_\ell}\cdot e(x)$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\nmid L'$, and $e(X_{U_{i}}\cdot x)=X_{U_{i}}\cdot e(x)$ for every $i\in\mathrm{Fin}(t)$, matching the $i$-th generator at level $L$ with the $i$-th at level $L'$.
--
--   This is the $\alpha$-stabilisation, or level-comparison, step at a single Taylor–Wiles prime for the cohomological modules of auxiliary level $\Gamma_0(NQ)\cap\Gamma_1(r)$, in the form where the diamond operators are already known to act trivially on the localisations, so that no Galois-theoretic input enters. It is used, by iteration over the primes of the Taylor–Wiles set, in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_linearEquiv_ML_HR_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_linearEquiv_ML_HR_auxLevel_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
